WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.180
While running an errand
for Director Sakuragi,

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.500
Satoshi, Go, and Koharu visited
Kuchiba City’s Pokémon Center.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.650
Thank you for waiting.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.190
Here are the supplements
you requested.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.970
Thank you!

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.290
That’s what we need
for the errand, then?

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.040
Yeah.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.700
Huh? Where’s Sarunori?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.270
Huh?

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.810
Sorry about that!

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.550
Stop, Eevee!

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.450
How is it your Sarunori always
ends up making mischief?

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.830
It’s always raring to play!

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.460
Your Eevee’s the same way.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.880
Really?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.840
Compared to Eevee,
Sarunori seems really childish...

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.300
Eevee tries to copy everything she sees.
That’s childish, too.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.300
Eevee always behaves
when she’s alone with me.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.800
Sarunori can behave, too!

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.270
Look out!

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.460
The cars, the cars,
the cars, the cars!

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.700
Well, you can’t call that behaving...

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.190
Ahh!

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.700
But she’s sweet, and she’s smart,
and cute!

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.200
Sarunori is sweet, smart,
and cute, too!

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.850
Well then, why not have them do the rest of the errand
so they can show us what they’ve got?

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.090
Th-The errand?

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.630
What now?

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.640
You could do that,
right, Pikachu?

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.090
So can Eevee!

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.090
So can Sarunori!

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.910
Now, these are very important.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.260
So make sure you take them back to Dad,
without losing them.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.710
See this?

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:54.790
You start here, and when you make it
up the hill at the end,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.300
you’ll be at the Sakuragi Institute!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.800
Got it?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.880
Don’t get sidetracked.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.220
Sarunori...
I know you can do it!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.700
Eevee...
It’s all up to you!

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:17.200
All right, Sarunori and
Eevee’s first errand...

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.150
...starts now!

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.140
Go, go!

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.690
Take care!

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.100
I’m really worried about them.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:28.950
Yeah...

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.950
What are you two doing?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.510
Quick, after them!

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:33.250
Huh?

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.780
After them?

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.460
Yeah!

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.840
You want them to succeed, right?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.810
If it looks like something
might go wrong,

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.490
we can give them some
sneaky full power backup!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.600
I get it now!

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:51.320
Plus, I can show you how sweet,
smart, and cute Sarunori is!

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:56.440
Then I’ll show off how sweet,
smart, and cute Eevee is, too.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.210
Time for the first...

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.130
No Matter What Pokémon Pops Out,

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:09.820
We’ll Be Ready To Battle With It...

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.410
Training Session!

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.470
Rocket...

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.240
Vending...

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:24.010
Secret!

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.680
What are we getting?!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.770
The Apple Juice Pokémon,
Tarpple!

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:38.390
Something smells great, meow...

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.270
Why?

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.130
What? You’re asking me?

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.050
Yep.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.280
All right...

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.410
Let’s see...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.600
Tarpple is...
Grass/Dragon type.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.670
Says its body is covered
in sweet nectar.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.020
Looking at this thing
is making me crave some...

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.580
Same here!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.000
What’re we gonna get?

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.380
The Fresh Snow Pokémon,
Vanipetit!

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.380
H-H-H-H-Hold on a sec!

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.940
Kojiro, where’s Morpeko?

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.980
Over there. Why?

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:20.140
It stuffed itself eating us out of snacks again,
then fell asleep, meow!

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:22.980
Nice timing!

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.870
Watch this, guys.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.200
W-What the...?!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.210
Vanipetit-on-Tarpple!

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.220
Yeah!

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:38.540
A perfect recreation of a
hot and tasty apple pie topped with vanilla ice cream.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.320
You’re right...

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:44.970
I can’t help it...

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:49.300
I’m already savoring the hot and tasty
apple pie topped with vanilla ice cream...

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.570
Same here, meow!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:57.770
Now I really want some hot and tasty apple pie
topped with vanilla ice cream, meow...

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.300
I know, right?

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.090
So, I thought this might happen...

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.180
And got us an apple pie!

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.330
Whoa!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:21.580
Sooo... Why don’t we go buy
some vanilla ice cream while it’s asleep,

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.790
and have this for snack time?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.090
Agreed!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.320
Okay then, go buy us
some vanilla ice cream.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.460
Right! Buy us some, now.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.540
Bring it straight back, meow!

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.440
Hold it, hold it, hold it!

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:45.610
Pelipper, are you really
up to running errands?

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:52.690
Hey, wait... Uh, what...?
Hey, wait! Hey!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.310
What did it say?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:58.700
“Leave it to me,” meow!

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:02.710
Really?! I’m, like,
<i>sooo</i> worried, though!

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.300
Looks like they’re doing well.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.800
They’re going the right way.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.640
Yeah, you’re right.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.270
Look!

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.170
It’s an Ishitsubute!

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.640
Not good...
That look on Sarunori’s face...

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:23.450
That’s its time-for-mischief grin!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.120
Not that way! You’ll get lost!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.660
Leave it to me.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.290
Come on out, Gänger!

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.690
We’ll give them some
sneaky full power backup!

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.080
We’re counting on you.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.420
This way! We’ll cut them off!

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.930
Gänger, go for it!
Psychokinesis!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.200
Not that way!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.460
H-Hold on...

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:36.150
Uh... Don’t scare them,
just get them back to the road.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.640
What a relief!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.610
So? Did they come back?

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.200
They went too far...

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.750
All right,
Pelipper hasn’t noticed us following it.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.980
I got worried enough to
follow it all the way here,

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.310
but it’s actually doing fine?

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.490
If it just goes straight down this road,
then takes the first right,

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.320
the ice cream shop’s
right there, meow!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.650
You can do it, Pelipper!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.950
This errand’s like taking candy
from a Bayleaf, Pelipper!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:51.550
Oh, no...

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.300
That’s its
“I forgot everything” face...

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.790
We’ll have to give it some
full power backup!

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.720
Ooooh!
You little whippersnapper!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.680
I have something to give you.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.180
Here, it’s a map to
the ice cream shop.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:12.190
Go straight down this road!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:17.150
Go straight, then turn right,
and the ice cream shop’s right there!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.860
Straight, then right!
Right, meow!

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:25.110
Just look at the map
and you’ll get there, meow.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:29.370
Right! Keep your eyes
glued to the map, that’ll do it!

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:32.880
The map!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.130
Huh?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.760
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.030
I knew it...

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:47.260
It really did keep its eyes glued
to the map, meow...

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:50.520
This errand’s doomed to fail,
isn’t it?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.020
No! I’m not giving in yet!

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:57.020
We’ll just have to hit it hard
with our trump card!

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:05.990
Looks like they’re gonna make it back
to the Institute before dark!

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.040
Ah! Look!

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.500
That’s a pretty big road!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.160
Will they really be okay...?

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.390
They’re looking right, looking left,
then looking right again!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:32.770
That’s perfect!

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.980
Just keep going,
and make it across!

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.430
You’re nearly there...
Nearly there!

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:44.910
<i>What?!</i>

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:47.850
Look out!

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.370
Wh-What do we do?!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.660
Sneaky full power backup!

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.190
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.390
Come on out,
Negigaknight!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.850
Stop that Pelipper!

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.740
All right!

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:33.230
That was close...

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.350
Yeah...

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:37.710
They’re crouched down!

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.100
D-D-Did they get hurt somehow?!

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.170
Or a stomachache or something?!

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.180
Just wait there! I’m coming!

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:52.100
They were just looking at
a Digda hole...

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.000
Ice cream! Ice cream!

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.070
Anyone looking for
some tasty vanilla ice cream?!

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.400
Vanilla ice cream!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:11.410
Any Pelipper out on an errand
to buy vanilla ice cream, head this way!

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:29.140
Now, these are very important.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.430
Eevee... It’s all up to you!

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:38.520
Eevee...

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.530
Hurry, hurry!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:45.230
Never expected <i>we’d</i> end up
selling it the ice cream...

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:50.530
Or rather, we could’ve just <i>eaten</i> this ice cream
in the first place, meow.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:50.530
Ice cream! Tasty ice cream!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.580
Ice cream!

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:54.910
Oh, welcome!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:15:00.630
Are you here for this vanilla ice cream
shaped like a Vanipetit?

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.240
Oh, you must be!

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:04.090
You want vanilla ice cream,
right?

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.550
Your vanilla ice cream!
Thanks for waiting!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:13.230
<i>Thank you for your patronage!</i>

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:17.400
Any Pelipper out on errands
should remember to head straight home!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.930
Sarunori...

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.250
Go!

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.780
Koharu, you head back
to the Institute without us!

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:44.750
Uh, sure!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:48.760
Eevee...

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.520
You’ve got this, Eevee!

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.060
A Kabigon!

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:25.420
Huh?

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.670
It’s gone...

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:57.240
Eevee... You <i>are</i> going to
be okay, right?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:04.610
Somehow, we managed to
make it back before Pelipper...

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:06.910
The apple pie’s safe too, meow.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:13.090
That’s enough...
You don’t have to stay posed like that.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.340
Welcome back!

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:23.100
How’d your errand go?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.460
Amazing, Pelipper!

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.980
See? You can do it if you try!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:35.300
Now, to put this on here,
and it’s ready, meow!

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:39.410
<i>A hot and tasty apple pie
topped with vanilla ice cream!</i>

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.110
Sarunori...
I know you can do it!

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:06.410
I hope Eevee didn’t go
the wrong way...

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:10.620
So you never found
Sarunori, then?

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.790
Right...

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:12.420
But...

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.550
Eevee!

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:21.050
Welcome back!

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.060
You really held on to them
any way you could!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.560
Well done, Eevee!

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.760
Great to see it, Koharu.

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:35.870
Yeah!

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:39.380
But Sarunori still isn’t back...

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.580
Don’t worry.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:52.290
Sarunori...

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.640
Hold on!

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.530
You’ve got this, Sarunori!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:23.440
You’re nearly there.
You’re so close!

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.700
Just a few more steps
and you’re home!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:35.960
That’s it!

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.800
You can do this!
You can do this, Sarunori!

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:40.650
Sarunori!

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.820
Wow...

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:58.370
You worked so hard!
That’s amazing, Sarunori!

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.950
You really did it!

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:16.510
All right!

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:21.200
That’s Eevee and Sarunori’s
first errand... Complete!

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:22.560
You did it!

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:33.250
Despite all their troubles...

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:37.340
Sarunori and Eevee have grown a little
through their first errand,

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:41.370
and perhaps Go and Koharu
have, too.

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.910
Go!

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:13.950
Ahh! My dinner’s gone again!

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:15.460
So is mine, meow!

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:17.450
Can’t we do something
about that thing, Kojiro?!

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:19.200
How am I supposed to know
what to do about it...?

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:22.750
<i>Ack!</i>

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:26.060
Oh, it’s fine,
you can keep eating...

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:28.570
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:31.100
Please! Catch Morpeko!!

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:33.340
Let’s just get it out of our hair
and back to the wild!
